== 3. Adverse Providences

#strong[The third #emph[device] that Satan has to keep the soul in a sad, doubting, and questioning condition, is,]

BY leading the soul to draw false#footnote[Ps 77:7, 11. Ps 88:1–18. Ps 73:2, 23.] inferences from the adverse actings of providence. Satan says, “Do you not see how providence thwarts your prayers, and thwarts your desires, your tears, your hopes, your endeavors? Surely, if his love were toward you, if his soul delighted and took pleasure in you, he would not deal with you this way,” etc.

#strong[Now the remedies against this device of Satan are as follows.]

The first #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is solemnly to consider that many things may be contrary to our desires that are not contrary to our good. Abraham, Jacob, David, Job, Moses, Jeremiah,#footnote[The Circumcellians, not being able to withstand the preaching and writing of Augustine, sought his destruction, and beset the road he was to take on his pastoral visit; but by God’s providence he missed his way and escaped the danger.] Jonah, Paul, etc. met with many things that were contrary to their desires and endeavors, that were not contrary to their good, as all know who have wisely compared their desires and endeavors with God’s actings. Medicine often works contrary to the patient’s desires when it does not work contrary to his good. I remember a story of a godly man who had a great desire to go to France. As he was going to take ship, he broke his leg; and it pleased providence so to order it that the ship he would have gone in was wrecked at that very time, and not a man saved; and so by breaking a bone his life was saved. Though providence worked against his desires, yet it did not work against his good, etc.

The second #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is solemnly to consider that the hand of God may be against a man when the love and heart of God are much set on that man. No man can conclude how the heart of God stands by his hand. The hand of God was against Ephraim, and yet his love, his heart, was#footnote[Jer 31:18, 19, 20. God’s providential hand may be with persons when his heart is set against them. God’s providential hand was for a time with Saul, Haman, Ashur, and Jehu, and yet his heart was set against them. “No man knows love or hatred by all that is before him” (Eccl 9:1, 2).] dearly set on Ephraim: “I have surely heard Ephraim’s moaning: ‘You disciplined me severely, like an untrained calf. Restore me, that I may return, for You are the #smallcaps[Lord] my God. After I returned, I repented; and after I was instructed, I struck my thigh in grief. I was ashamed and humiliated because I bore the disgrace of my youth.’ Is not Ephraim a dear son to Me, a delightful child? Though I often speak against him, I still remember him. Therefore My heart yearns for him; I have great compassion for him,” declares the #smallcaps[Lord].

God can look sourly, and chide bitterly, and strike heavily, even where and when he loves dearly. The hand of God was very much against Job, and yet his love, his heart, was very much set on Job, as you may see by comparing the first two chapters of Job with the last two. The hand of God was heavy against David and Jonah when his heart was much set on them. He who concludes that the heart of God is against those whom his hand is against will condemn the generation of the just, whom God would not have anyone condemn unjustly.

The third #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is to consider that all the adverse providences that befall the saints are only in order to some noble good that God intends to confer on them. Providence worked against David’s desire in taking away the child sinfully conceived, but yet not against a more noble good. For was it not far better for David to have such a lawful heir as Solomon was, than that a bastard should wear the crown and wield the scepter?

Joseph, you know, was sold into a far country by the envy and malice of his brothers, and afterwards imprisoned because he would not be a prisoner to the lusts of his master’s wife. Yet all these adverse providences wonderfully served his advancement, and the preservation of his father’s family, which was then the visible church of Christ. It was so ordered by a noble hand of providence that what they sought to prevent, they promoted. Joseph was sold by his brothers so that he would not be bowed down to, and yet he was bowed down to because he was sold.

David was appointed to a kingdom; but oh, the straits, troubles, and dangers of death that he ran through before he felt the weight of the crown! And all this was only in order to sweeten his crown, and to settle it more firmly and gloriously on his head. God so contrived it that Jonah’s offense, and those contrary actings of his that attended it, should advance the very end they seemed most directly#footnote[The workings of divine providence are so dark, so deep, so changeable, that the wisest and noblest souls cannot tell what conclusions to draw.] to oppose. Jonah flees to Tarshish, is then cast into the sea, then saved by a miracle. Then the mariners who cast Jonah into the sea, as is very probable, declared to the Ninevites what had happened: that therefore he must be a man sent by God, and that his threatenings must be believed and heeded, and therefore they must repent and humble themselves, so that the wrath threatened might not be carried out, etc.

The fourth #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is seriously to consider that all the strange, dark, deep, and changeable providences that believers meet with will further them in their way to heaven, in their journey to happiness. Divine wisdom and love will so order all things here below that they will work for the real, internal, and eternal good of those who love him. All the rugged providences that David met with contributed to#footnote[Orosius, speaking of Valentinian, says that he who for Christ’s name’s sake had lost a tribuneship, a while after succeeded his persecutor in the empire.] bringing him to the throne; and all the rugged providences that Daniel and the three young men met with contributed to their great advancement. So all the rugged providences that believers meet with will all contribute to the lifting up of their souls above all things below God. As the waters lifted Noah’s ark nearer heaven, and as all the stones that flew about Stephen’s ears only knocked him closer to Christ, the cornerstone, so all the strange, rugged providences that we meet with will raise us nearer heaven, and knock us nearer to Christ, that precious cornerstone, etc.
